WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.453 --> 00:00:17.924
The police station was nearby, so the crowd could only accompany Oliver through two or three streets.

2
00:00:19.005 --> 00:00:22.969
But even that short distance seemed to please a tall man wrapped in a dark cloak.

3
00:00:24.070 --> 00:00:28.513
As Oliver was led into the court, the man's lips curled in a cruel smile.

4
00:00:29.554 --> 00:00:31.216
He disappeared when the crowd broke up.

5
00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:33.641
Oliver was taken to a cell.

6
00:00:34.662 --> 00:00:38.846
The old gentleman whose handkerchief had been stolen was instructed to wait in a small room.

7
00:00:38.866 --> 00:00:43.990
"There's something about that boy's face that touches me," the old gentleman said to himself.

8
00:00:44.891 --> 00:00:45.891
"Could he be innocent?

9
00:00:46.752 --> 00:00:48.333
Where have I seen that face before?"

10
00:00:49.414 --> 00:00:52.317
The old gentleman thought back over the many people he'd known.

11
00:00:52.337 --> 00:00:54.759
"No," he said at last.

12
00:00:54.779 --> 00:00:57.281
"It must be my imagination."

13
00:00:58.362 --> 00:01:01.044
He picked up the book from the bookshop and started reading again.

14
00:01:02.180 --> 00:01:03.761
Soon he was led into the courtroom.

15
00:01:04.821 --> 00:01:09.583
Mr. Fang, the magistrate, sat at one end of the room while Oliver sat trembling in a wooden

16
00:01:09.643 --> 00:01:12.504
pen. "Who are you?"

17
00:01:12.925 --> 00:01:14.245
Mr. Fang demanded gruffly.

18
00:01:14.265 --> 00:01:17.386
"My name is Brownlow," said the old gentleman.

19
00:01:17.406 --> 00:01:20.788
"And what crime are you charged with?"

20
00:01:20.808 --> 00:01:23.309
"I'm not charged with any crime!

21
00:01:24.429 --> 00:01:25.770
My handkerchief was stolen."

22
00:01:26.910 --> 00:01:28.871
"Swear this man in," Mr.

23
00:01:28.911 --> 00:01:30.332
Fang instructed a court officer.

24
00:01:31.380 --> 00:01:32.080
And so Mr.

25
00:01:32.120 --> 00:01:33.541
Brownlow began to tell his story.

26
00:01:34.541 --> 00:01:38.003
He explained that he had chased Oliver because he saw the boy running away.

27
00:01:39.123 --> 00:01:43.705
He hoped the magistrate would be lenient if this boy wasn't the thief but merely connected with thieves.

28
00:01:44.906 --> 00:01:45.926
In conclusion Mr.

29
00:01:45.966 --> 00:01:48.207
Brownlow said, "The boy has been hurt already."

30
00:01:49.268 --> 00:01:53.750
Then looking at Oliver, he said forcefully, "And I fear I really fear that he's ill."

31
00:01:53.770 --> 00:01:57.911
"Oh, yes, I'm sure he's ill," said Mr.

32
00:01:57.952 --> 00:01:58.732
Fang with a sneer.

33
00:02:00.512 --> 00:02:05.714
He looked at Oliver and said sternly, "I'll have none of your tricks here, you young vagabond.

34
00:02:06.814 --> 00:02:07.754
What's your name?"

35
00:02:08.915 --> 00:02:11.235
Oliver tried to reply, but his tongue failed him.

36
00:02:12.336 --> 00:02:15.296
The whole room seemed to spin, and he was deadly pale.

37
00:02:15.316 --> 00:02:18.657
"What's your name, you hardened scoundrel?"

38
00:02:18.898 --> 00:02:19.578
demanded Mr.

39
00:02:19.618 --> 00:02:22.459
Fang. "Officer, what's his name?"

40
00:02:23.579 --> 00:02:26.740
This comment was addressed to a police officer standing next to Oliver.

41
00:02:27.828 --> 00:02:30.490
The policeman bent over the boy and repeated the question.

42
00:02:31.471 --> 00:02:33.632
But he realized that Oliver couldn't reply.

43
00:02:34.653 --> 00:02:39.076
He also knew that this would make the magistrate angry and likely add to the severity of Oliver's

44
00:02:39.116 --> 00:02:44.700
punishment. "He says his name's Tom White, your worship," replied the kindhearted police officer.

45
00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:46.921
"Where does he live?"

46
00:02:47.361 --> 00:02:47.842
asked Mr.

47
00:02:47.882 --> 00:02:54.226
Fang. "Wherever he can, your worship," replied the officer, again pretending to hear Oliver's answer.

48
00:02:54.246 --> 00:02:56.748
"Does he have any parents?"

49
00:02:57.984 --> 00:03:01.825
"He says they died in his infancy, your worship," said the officer, making a guess.

50
00:03:03.006 --> 00:03:06.687
At this point Oliver raised his head and looked around with imploring eyes.

51
00:03:06.707 --> 00:03:09.828
"Please, may I have a drink of water?"

52
00:03:10.108 --> 00:03:10.968
he asked feebly.

53
00:03:10.988 --> 00:03:13.849
"Stuff and nonsense!"

54
00:03:14.329 --> 00:03:14.749
said Mr.

55
00:03:14.789 --> 00:03:17.770
Fang. "Don't try to make a fool of me."

56
00:03:17.790 --> 00:03:21.411
"I think he really is ill, Your Worship," said the officer.

57
00:03:21.431 --> 00:03:24.212
"I know better," said Mr.

58
00:03:24.252 --> 00:03:25.860
Fang. Mr.

59
00:03:25.900 --> 00:03:27.881
Brownlow had been watching Oliver with concern.

60
00:03:27.901 --> 00:03:30.061
"Take care of him, Officer.

61
00:03:31.102 --> 00:03:31.842
He'll fall down."

62
00:03:31.862 --> 00:03:35.023
"Step back, Officer," said Mr.

63
00:03:35.083 --> 00:03:37.883
Fang. "Let him fall if he likes."

64
00:03:39.104 --> 00:03:41.784
And with that, Oliver fainted and fell to the floor.

65
00:03:43.425 --> 00:03:46.966
The men in the room looked at each other, but no one dared to move without Mr.

66
00:03:47.006 --> 00:03:47.806
Fang's permission.

67
00:03:47.826 --> 00:03:50.887
"I knew he was pretending," Mr.

68
00:03:50.927 --> 00:03:52.767
Fang said in a self-satisfied way.

69
00:03:52.787 --> 00:03:54.728
"Let him lie there.

70
00:03:55.660 --> 00:03:57.822
He'll soon grow tired of his game and get up."

71
00:03:57.842 --> 00:04:00.584
"How do you propose to deal with the case, sir?"

72
00:04:00.944 --> 00:04:02.185
asked the clerk in a low voice.

73
00:04:02.205 --> 00:04:06.309
"He is committed to prison for three months," said Mr.

74
00:04:06.349 --> 00:04:09.792
Fang. "And sentenced to hard labor, of course.

75
00:04:10.873 --> 00:04:12.254
Everyone, clear the courtroom."

76
00:04:13.335 --> 00:04:17.558
The door was opened and a couple of men prepared to carry the unconscious boy to his cell.

77
00:04:18.659 --> 00:04:22.262
Suddenly an old man rushed into the courtroom and advanced toward the magistrate.

78
00:04:22.282 --> 00:04:24.604
"Stop, stop!

79
00:04:25.548 --> 00:04:26.689
Don't take him away!"

80
00:04:27.710 --> 00:04:29.611
The new arrival was breathless with hurry.

81
00:04:29.631 --> 00:04:31.573
"What is this?

82
00:04:32.574 --> 00:04:33.294
Who is this?

83
00:04:34.315 --> 00:04:35.456
Turn this man out.

84
00:04:36.497 --> 00:04:37.678
Clear the courtroom!"

85
00:04:38.018 --> 00:04:38.519
cried Mr.

86
00:04:38.579 --> 00:04:42.562
Fang. "I will speak," declared the man.

87
00:04:42.582 --> 00:04:44.764
"I will not be turned away.

88
00:04:45.845 --> 00:04:46.926
I saw everything.

89
00:04:47.967 --> 00:04:48.807
I own the bookshop.

90
00:04:49.808 --> 00:04:51.670
I demand that you hear my evidence, Mr.

91
00:04:51.710 --> 00:04:54.312
Fang. You must not refuse me."

92
00:04:55.360 --> 00:04:57.881
The man stood in front of the bench, breathing heavily.

93
00:04:58.981 --> 00:05:00.922
"Swear him in," growled Mr.

94
00:05:01.002 --> 00:05:04.763
Fang. "Now, man, what have you got to say?"

95
00:05:04.783 --> 00:05:07.823
"This gentleman was reading outside my shop."

96
00:05:08.844 --> 00:05:09.884
The man indicated Mr.

97
00:05:09.924 --> 00:05:15.746
Brownlow. "I saw three boys—two others and the prisoner here—loitering across the way.

98
00:05:16.766 --> 00:05:18.766
The robbery was committed by another boy.

99
00:05:19.947 --> 00:05:24.348
I saw it, and I also saw that this boy was perfectly amazed and stupefied by it."

100
00:05:25.428 --> 00:05:30.570
The bookshop owner took a deep breath and then proceeded to relate the exact circumstances of the robbery.

101
00:05:31.671 --> 00:05:33.231
Mr. Fang was clearly annoyed.

102
00:05:33.251 --> 00:05:36.013
"Why didn't you come here before?"

103
00:05:36.033 --> 00:05:39.794
"I didn't have anyone to mind the shop," replied the man.

104
00:05:39.814 --> 00:05:43.936
"Everybody who could have helped me had joined in the chase.

105
00:05:45.076 --> 00:05:48.598
I couldn't get anybody until five minutes ago, and I've run all the way here."

106
00:05:48.618 --> 00:05:51.179
"This man was reading, was he?"

107
00:05:51.499 --> 00:05:52.740
Mr. Fang pointed to Mr.

108
00:05:52.760 --> 00:05:56.186
Brownlow. "Yes, the very book he has in his hand."

109
00:05:56.206 --> 00:05:58.048
"Oh, that book.

110
00:05:59.089 --> 00:05:59.990
Is it paid for?"

111
00:06:00.010 --> 00:06:03.973
"No, it is not," said the bookseller with a smile.

112
00:06:03.993 --> 00:06:07.216
"Dear me, I forgot all about that!"

113
00:06:07.597 --> 00:06:08.257
exclaimed Mr.

114
00:06:08.277 --> 00:06:13.662
Brownlow. "Well, you're a nice person to bring charges against a poor boy!"

115
00:06:13.963 --> 00:06:14.383
said Mr.

116
00:06:14.423 --> 00:06:19.488
Fang. "You obtained that book under very suspicious and disreputable circumstances.

117
00:06:20.584 --> 00:06:24.126
You're lucky that the owner of that book has decided not to prosecute you.

118
00:06:25.206 --> 00:06:26.567
Let this be a lesson to you."

119
00:06:26.587 --> 00:06:29.108
"What! But I meant to pay!"

120
00:06:29.508 --> 00:06:30.088
exclaimed Mr.

121
00:06:30.128 --> 00:06:33.089
Brownlow. "The boy is discharged.

122
00:06:34.130 --> 00:06:35.230
Clear the courtroom!"

123
00:06:35.590 --> 00:06:36.031
said Mr.

124
00:06:36.091 --> 00:06:39.312
Fang. "Officers, do you hear?

125
00:06:40.372 --> 00:06:41.353
Clear the courtroom."

126
00:06:42.393 --> 00:06:43.234
An indignant Mr.

127
00:06:43.274 --> 00:06:48.216
Brownlow was escorted from the magistrate's court with the book in one hand and his bamboo cane in

128
00:06:48.256 --> 00:06:48.596
the other.

129
00:06:49.580 --> 00:06:52.121
But when he reached the pavement, his rage evaporated.

130
00:06:53.221 --> 00:06:57.702
Little Oliver Twist lay on the ground with his shirt unbuttoned and his face a deadly white.

131
00:06:57.722 --> 00:07:00.543
"Poor boy, poor boy!"

132
00:07:00.903 --> 00:07:01.283
said Mr.

133
00:07:01.323 --> 00:07:02.444
Brownlow, bending over him.

134
00:07:02.464 --> 00:07:04.524
"Call a coach, somebody."

135
00:07:05.564 --> 00:07:08.305
A coach arrived and Oliver was carefully laid on one seat.

136
00:07:09.365 --> 00:07:11.406
Mr. Brownlow got in and sat on the other one.

137
00:07:11.426 --> 00:07:13.427
"May I accompany you?"

138
00:07:13.767 --> 00:07:15.147
said the bookseller, looking in.

139
00:07:15.167 --> 00:07:18.148
"Bless me, yes, my dear sir," said Mr.

140
00:07:18.188 --> 00:07:20.889
Brownlow. "I still have this unhappy book.

141
00:07:21.829 --> 00:07:22.229
Jump in.

142
00:07:23.170 --> 00:07:23.770
Poor fellow!

143
00:07:24.630 --> 00:07:25.711
There's no time to lose."

144
00:07:26.731 --> 00:07:30.113
The bookseller got into the coach, and away they drove toward Mr.

145
00:07:30.153 --> 00:07:30.913
Brownlow's home.
